    Overrides the python generator's built-in README.mustache. Passed as
    -t templates/python; templates absent from that directory fall back to the
    ones embedded in the jar, which is why only this file exists.

    NOTE: a mustache comment ends at its first closing brace pair, so no
    variable or partial tag may appear in this block. Naming one here silently
    ends the comment and renders the remainder as markup.

    Three defects in the built-in template motivated the override. It installs
    from a git URL rather than the registry the package is published to; it
    documents `python setup.py install`, which setuptools removed; and it
    advertises pytest to run tests MANIFEST.in prunes from the distribution.

    Omitted deliberately: the build-date line, which would churn this file on
    every run, and the build-package line, which names an internal generator
    class.

    The trailing common_README partial is the generator's own, carrying the
    usage example and the endpoint, model and authorization tables.
